1
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:06,000
Infinite space. Infinite terror.

2
00:08:00,000 --> 00:08:06,000
Event Horizon is a horror, science fiction, mystery
film directed by Paul W. S. Anderson.

3
00:12:00,000 --> 00:12:06,000
In 2047, a group of astronauts are sent to investigate and salvage the starship Event
Horizon which disappeared mysteriously seven years before on its maiden voyage.

4
00:16:00,000 --> 00:16:06,000
However, it soon becomes evident that something
sinister resides in its corridors.

5
00:20:00,000 --> 00:20:06,000
Miller, played by Laurence Fishburne.

6
00:24:00,000 --> 00:24:06,000
Weir, played by Sam Neill.

7
00:28:00,000 --> 00:28:06,000
Peters, played by Kathleen Quinlan.

8
00:32:00,000 --> 00:32:06,000
Starck, played by Joely Richardson.

9
00:36:00,000 --> 00:36:06,000
Cooper, played by Richard T. Jones.

10
00:40:00,000 --> 00:40:06,000
Justin, played by Jack Noseworthy.

11
00:44:00,000 --> 00:44:06,000
Event Horizon is a 1997 science fiction horror film directed
by Paul Anderson and written by Philip Eisner.

12
00:48:00,000 --> 00:48:06,000
It stars Laurence Fishburne, Sam Neill, Kathleen Quinlan, and Joely Richardson.

13
00:52:00,000 --> 00:52:06,000
The film follows a crew of astronauts in the year 2047 who are sent on a rescue mission after the Event Horizon, a
spaceship that went missing seven years earlier, spontaneously reappears in orbit around Neptune.

14
00:56:00,000 --> 00:56:06,000
The film had a troubled production, with filming and editing rushed by Paramount Pictures
when it became clear that Titanic would not meet its projected release.

15
01:00:00,000 --> 01:00:06,000
The original 130-minute cut of the film was heavily edited by the
studio's demand, much to Anderson's consternation.

16
01:04:00,000 --> 01:04:06,000
Event Horizon was released in the United States on 15 August
1997 and the United Kingdom one week later.

17
01:08:00,000 --> 01:08:06,000
It was a commercial and critical failure, grossing
$42 million on a $60 million budget.

18
01:12:00,000 --> 01:12:06,000
However, it sold well on home video; its initial DVD release sold so well that Paramount contacted Anderson to
begin working on a restoration of the deleted footage, but it had been either lost or destroyed.

19
01:16:00,000 --> 01:16:06,000
The film has since been reassessed as a cult classic that influenced many sci-fi and horror films
and video games, and has appeared on lists of the best horror films of all time.

20
01:20:00,000 --> 01:20:06,000
In 2025, Event Horizon: Dark Descent, a comic book prequel
series began being published by IDW Publishing.

21
01:24:00,000 --> 01:24:06,000
In 2026, Event Horizon: Inferno, a comic book sequel series, is
set to begin being published by IDW Publishing.

22
01:28:00,000 --> 01:28:06,000
The film explores themes of space marine, nightmare,
insanity, delusion, hallucination.

23
01:32:00,000 --> 01:32:06,000
The tone is dark and thought_provoking and mind_bending.
